01:26:45.911 --> 01:26:49.559
there's a belief that the community is working hard,

01:26:49.727 --> 01:26:52.951
but the city is not backing it up. And I think we need

01:26:52.983 --> 01:26:55.615
to show that that is not true.

01:27:00.635 --> 01:27:04.091
Okay, almost doing a point of personal

01:27:04.203 --> 01:27:07.415
privilege there, but just be quiet.

01:27:09.715 --> 01:27:13.267
O'Rourke. Thanks America.

01:27:13.291 --> 01:27:16.443
Through staff, a question actually, and I

01:27:16.459 --> 01:27:19.835
would disagree with Councillor Alts last point. The city

01:27:19.875 --> 01:27:23.291
is doing millions upon millions upon millions for affordable

01:27:23.363 --> 01:27:28.383
housing basic needs. Where I sit on that TAS task force and

01:27:28.479 --> 01:27:31.767
know the affordability of property taxes also is felt by

01:27:31.791 --> 01:27:35.035
these organizations through their rent or if they own their building.

01:27:36.495 --> 01:27:39.679
So I would just point that out and that the city, in fact, has done

01:27:39.767 --> 01:27:42.995
quite a lot. My question to staff,

01:27:43.615 --> 01:27:47.559
I actually thought when we heard the groups, they were saying the arts funding

01:27:47.607 --> 01:27:51.155
was still being conflated in the overall pot.

01:27:51.545 --> 01:27:55.441
I thought there had been direction given previously to identify a

01:27:55.473 --> 01:27:59.377
stream where arts and culture was not competing with,

01:27:59.441 --> 01:28:02.685
say, you know, food security or that kind of thing.

01:28:03.465 --> 01:28:07.561
Are we going to see that differentiation in

01:28:07.593 --> 01:28:10.697
this round or is that part of the work

01:28:10.721 --> 01:28:12.485
that's coming in 2026?

01:28:14.265 --> 01:28:18.009
Through the merit of Counselor O'Rourke? It's my understanding of the history that

01:28:18.057 --> 01:28:20.997
previously community grants were separated into streams where,

01:28:21.021 --> 01:28:24.101
for example, arts and culture had a stream. And then there was a review that

01:28:24.133 --> 01:28:27.821
took place perhaps four or five years ago where

01:28:27.853 --> 01:28:31.709
it was determined that the most flexible and most responsive

01:28:31.757 --> 01:28:34.925
approach to community need in any given year was for there to be one

01:28:34.965 --> 01:28:38.357
pot. And so those streams within the pot or

01:28:38.381 --> 01:28:42.485
the envelope were eliminated. And that's why we've certainly

01:28:42.525 --> 01:28:45.785
heard the feedback from the arts and culture community

01:28:46.115 --> 01:28:49.947
recently. But that is. That's why we want to undertake a

01:28:49.971 --> 01:28:53.899
review in 2026 to, to better understand,

01:28:54.067 --> 01:28:58.315
was the move to have just one envelope and be more responsive to community

01:28:58.395 --> 01:29:01.971
need in any given year from any given sector the right

01:29:02.003 --> 01:29:05.267
thing to do, and is it working, or do we need to return to

01:29:05.291 --> 01:29:08.755
the previous approach. Okay, I thought

01:29:08.795 --> 01:29:11.055
that was happening already, so.

01:29:11.835 --> 01:29:13.185
Okay. Thanks.

01:29:17.485 --> 01:29:18.785
Councillor Gibson.

01:29:21.605 --> 01:29:24.853
Thank you, Mr. Mayor. Just a comment. Just in defense of the

01:29:24.869 --> 01:29:28.533
work we are doing as a city, we could spend the

01:29:28.549 --> 01:29:32.485
better part of this day bringing up and talking about

01:29:32.605 --> 01:29:36.709
all of the grants, all of the funding,

01:29:36.797 --> 01:29:39.805
all of the community work that the city is doing.

01:29:40.905 --> 01:29:44.449
I don't think a comment like we're not doing enough should stand.

01:29:44.577 --> 01:29:48.001
So I just want to make that personal opinion that I don't believe that is

01:29:48.033 --> 01:29:52.001
accurate. There has been a debate ongoing,

01:29:52.113 --> 01:29:54.885
probably in this city for the last 35 years,

01:29:55.545 --> 01:29:58.937
and it continues. It's an ideological debate. I'm happy

01:29:58.961 --> 01:30:01.165
to be part of it, and I'm happy to counter.

01:30:02.425 --> 01:30:06.619
Western civilizations have had governments pop up everywhere

01:30:06.707 --> 01:30:10.411
for the last hundred years, insisting that if we could just increase taxation,

01:30:10.523 --> 01:30:13.795
we can eliminate poverty. It just makes the bread

01:30:13.835 --> 01:30:16.891
lines longer. And when you. When you tip over

01:30:16.923 --> 01:30:20.723
the affordability crisis, you just create longer lines for charity

01:30:20.819 --> 01:30:24.755
and for support. That's true. You have to allow people

01:30:24.915 --> 01:30:28.443
to afford the lifestyle that they're giving, that they're working towards.

01:30:28.579 --> 01:30:32.309
You cannot tax your way to prosperity. That's a platitude.

01:30:32.357 --> 01:30:36.253
But we're entering into that world now around this horseshoe where we are just.

01:30:36.429 --> 01:30:40.109
These are ideological platitudes that are coming out, and I'm just happy to counter that

01:30:40.157 --> 01:30:40.745
comment.

01:30:43.125 --> 01:30:49.025
Okay, I am going to call

01:30:49.885 --> 01:30:53.749
the vote on this now. I did, in listening

01:30:53.797 --> 01:30:57.277
