01:36:16.523 --> 01:36:19.635
there's a return on investment, economic tourism,

01:36:19.935 --> 01:36:23.111
civic pride. It's not just a piece of

01:36:23.143 --> 01:36:26.591
public art. It's what that art does to the community and for the

01:36:26.623 --> 01:36:29.275
community. Thank you.

01:36:29.735 --> 01:36:32.515
And then downer. I'm sorry, Caton. And then downer,

01:36:33.455 --> 01:36:36.863
thank you. Through you, Mr. Mayor, art is equity.

01:36:36.999 --> 01:36:40.815
Like, we got our rainbow crosswalk funded through public art.

01:36:40.975 --> 01:36:44.857
We can have indigenous art. We can celebrate the

01:36:45.031 --> 01:36:48.685
increasing number of cultures that we have in our community through art.

01:36:48.845 --> 01:36:52.077
I think that art is not just something pretty to look at.

01:36:52.101 --> 01:36:55.909
It's something that makes you feel something. And we need

01:36:55.957 --> 01:36:59.501
more of it in the city to include all of the population

01:36:59.573 --> 01:37:00.585
that lives here.

01:37:02.765 --> 01:37:05.785
Thank you, Downer. And then Bucito, please.

